\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item The caller supplies and pins the gene set. Use the primary-assembly GTF, not chr_patch_hapl_scaff: counting ALT haplotypes as genes made human release 116 look 6.99\% multi-gene when it is 0.36\% (mzLib EnsemblGeneSet remarks).
\item A FASTA carries no Ensembl links, so every FASTA protein is not_in_source regardless of biology; the result caveats count them.
\item Contaminants are never mapped (contaminant_not_mapped), even when they would resolve.
\item multi_gene is one row per gene, never a pick.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
}
